<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sayf al-Din Suri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1149</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sayf al-Din Suri was a prince of the Ghurid dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghor">Ghor</a>. After his brother Qutb al-Din Muhammad was poisoned at the Ghaznavid court, he seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazni">Ghazni</a> in 1148 and drove out <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Bahram Shah. Bahram Shah returned the next winter, captured him and had him executed, and his death prompted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ala-al-din-husayn">Ala al-Din Husayn</a> to sack Ghazni.</p></div>
